# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ',' and '&' compile successfully at M3 but require urbi_step driver
# (realm-managed strand) to run. The uvm_run REPL path has no realm; these
# opcodes produce a runtime TypeError in that context. The chk runner uses
# the REPL (uvm_run path), so we expect TypeError at runtime, not emit error.
# Real concurrent execution is tested via unit tests (test_fork.c).

1 , 2
[00000001] !!! TypeError: OP_FORK_DETACH: `,` requires urbi_step driver (realm == NULL)

1 & 2
[00000002] !!! TypeError: OP_FORK_JOIN: `&` requires urbi_step driver (realm == NULL)
